// Title: Run PowerShell Script from Redirected Input Stream
// Sigma ID: c83bf4b5-cdf0-437c-90fa-43d734f7c476
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Moriarty Meng (idea), Anton Kutepov (rule), oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-17 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects PowerShell script execution via input stream redirect
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/blob/4db780e0f0b2e2bb8cb1fa13e09196da9b9f1834/yml/LOLUtilz/OSBinaries/Powershell.yml
//   - https://twitter.com/Moriarty_Meng/status/984380793383370752
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_run_script_from_input_stream.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe") and ProcessCommandLine matches regex "\\s-\\s*<"
